        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2c555704-b338-5c09-83af-7babde746403",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Patsy Mink, Arlene Horowitz\n- Laws: Women's Educational Equity Act, P.L. 93-380\n- Places: Hawaii\n- Roles: Congresswoman, staff assistant\n- Organizations: United States House of Representatives, education subcommittee, Democratic Party\n\nFacts:\n- Patsy Matsu Takemoto Mink was born on December 6, 1927, and she was an American politician from Hawaii.\n- Patsy Mink was a third-generation Japanese American and a member of the Democratic Party.\n- The Women's Educational Equity Act was enacted as Section 513 of P.L. 93-380.\n- Congresswoman Patsy Mink of Hawaii introduced the Women's Educational Equity Act in the United States House of Representatives.\n- Arlene Horowitz, a staff assistant to the education subcommittee on which Patsy Mink served, conceived and drafted the Women's Educational Equity Act.\n- Patsy Matsu Takemoto Mink died on September 28, 2002.",
